1
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:38,500
I've taken your castle.

2
00:02:40,010 --> 00:02:42,510
- Theon? - It's Prince Theon now.

3
00:02:42,510 --> 00:02:44,720
Get up. You have to get dressed.

4
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:47,590
I've taken Winterfell.

5
00:02:47,930 --> 00:02:50,380
I took it. I'm occupying it.

6
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:53,370
I sent men over the walls with grappling claws and ropes.

7
00:02:53,370 --> 00:02:56,650
- Why? - To take the castle.

8
00:02:56,650 --> 00:03:00,370
- You went with Robb. - And he sent me back to Pyke.

9
00:03:01,020 --> 00:03:02,000
I'm a Greyjoy.

10
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,470
I can't fight for Robb and my father both.

11
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:08,800
- Where's Hodor? - I don't know.

12
00:03:08,930 --> 00:03:10,440
Find the halfwit.

13
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:14,520
My men are bringing your people together in the courtyard.

14
00:03:14,740 --> 00:03:15,670
Why?

15
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:17,530
So you and I can go down and tell them

16
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:20,550
- how you've yielded Winterfell to me. - I won't.

17
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,740
Yes, you will.

18
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:25,900
I won't. I'll never yield.

19
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,760
We'll fight you and throw you out.

20
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:35,180
The castle is mine,

21
00:03:35,490 --> 00:03:37,540
but these people are still yours.

22
00:03:37,710 --> 00:03:39,770
You'll yield to keep them safe,

23
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,630
to keep them alive.

24
00:03:42,660 --> 00:03:44,960
That's what a good lord would do.

25
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:50,990
Think carefully about what you want to say.

26
00:03:53,940 --> 00:03:55,330
Theon.

27
00:03:56,030 --> 00:03:57,910
Did you hate us the whole time?

28
00:04:05,970 --> 00:04:08,060
I've yielded Winterfell to Theon.

29
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:09,370
Louder.

30
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:11,410
Say Prince Theon.

31
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,760
I've yielded Winterfell to Prince Theon.

32
00:04:15,020 --> 00:04:16,530
You all know me.

33
00:04:16,530 --> 00:04:19,150
Aye, we know you for a steaming sack of shit.

34
00:04:19,150 --> 00:04:21,130
Farlen, you be silent.

35
00:04:21,130 --> 00:04:23,640
Listen to your little lord, Farlen.

36
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,920
He has more sense than you do.

37
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:28,010
All of you should do as he commands.

38
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:31,740
My father has donned the ancient crown of salt and rock

39
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:34,760
and declared himself King of the Iron Islands.

40
00:04:35,310 --> 00:04:38,400
He claims the North as well by right of conquest.

41
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,060
You are all his subjects.

42
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:42,990
Bugger that. I serve the Starks.

43
00:04:42,990 --> 00:04:46,360
- if you think you can hold the North with this-- - Shut up!

44
00:04:46,410 --> 00:04:50,050
If you serve me as loyally as you served Ned Stark,

45
00:04:50,050 --> 00:04:52,530
I will be as good to you as he ever was.

46
00:04:52,570 --> 00:04:55,240
Betray me, and you will wish you hadn't.

47
00:04:56,880 --> 00:05:00,100
Maester Luwin, send a raven to Pyke

48
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:02,830
informing my father of my victory here

49
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:05,400
and one to Deepwood Motte to my sister.

50
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:09,900
Inform her that she's to bring 500 men to Winterfell.

51
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:15,460
You are a Maester of the Citadel

52
00:05:15,590 --> 00:05:18,940
sworn to serve the lord of Winterfell, are you not?

53
00:05:19,230 --> 00:05:20,460
I am.

54
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:24,360
I am the Lord of Winterfell as Bran just informed you.

55
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:27,560
Send the ravens.

56
00:05:29,630 --> 00:05:31,180
My Lord.

57
00:05:33,410 --> 00:05:35,040
My Lord Greyjoy.

58
00:05:36,770 --> 00:05:39,710
I see you've finally learned how to address your betters.

59
00:05:40,970 --> 00:05:42,240
What do you want?

60
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:44,050
I was brought here a captive.

61
00:05:44,450 --> 00:05:46,570
You were here the day I was taken.

62
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:49,780
I'm the one who took you. What of it?

63
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:52,840
Let me serve you.

64
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:55,260
Serve me how?

65
00:05:55,770 --> 00:05:57,860
I need fighters, not kitchen sluts.

66
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,860
It was Robb Stark who put me in the kitchens.

67
00:06:01,730 --> 00:06:03,770
Put a spear in my hand again.

68
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:06,380
So you can bury it in my neck?

69
00:06:06,470 --> 00:06:08,150
Do you take me for a fool?

70
00:06:08,190 --> 00:06:09,460
Get up.

71
00:06:09,970 --> 00:06:11,310
Step aside.

72
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:14,320
Why?

73
00:06:15,910 --> 00:06:18,040
It's your dream, little Lord.

74
00:06:18,420 --> 00:06:21,240
The ocean has come to swallow this place.

75
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:23,600
I ain't letting it drown me.

76
00:06:24,230 --> 00:06:26,920
- And in a few days' time... - Greyjoy!

77
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:34,520
What have they done to him?

78
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:37,470
We caught this one on his way back from Torrhen's Square.

79
00:06:37,660 --> 00:06:40,390
Took out two of ours before I got his sword.

80
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:44,150
Ser Rodrik, it grieves me that we meet as foes.

81
00:06:44,150 --> 00:06:47,940
It grieves me you've less honor than a back alley whore.

82
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:50,730
You were raised here under this roof.

83
00:06:50,730 --> 00:06:53,990
- These people are your people. - They are not my people.

84
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:56,200
King Robb thought of you as a brother.

85
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,980
My brothers are dead.

86
00:06:59,030 --> 00:07:02,360
They died fighting Stark men, men like you.

87
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:05,080
Aye, they died fighting a war your father started.

88
00:07:05,520 --> 00:07:07,920
Lord Stark raised you among his own sons.

89
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,880
Among them, but not one of them.

90
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,950
I was his hostage taken from my home.

91
00:07:12,950 --> 00:07:14,330
If he were alive to see this--

92
00:07:14,330 --> 00:07:16,490
He's not. He's dead.

93
00:07:16,570 --> 00:07:18,700
The Seven Kingdoms are at war.

94
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:21,120
And Winterfell is mine.

95
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:23,450
I should have put a sword in your belly

96
00:07:23,450 --> 00:07:25,380
instead of in your hand.

97
00:07:25,780 --> 00:07:28,300
You've served this house faithfully, old man.

98
00:07:28,310 --> 00:07:30,400
But keep talking and I'll--

99
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,750
Take him to the cells. Lock him up--

100
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:36,220
My prince,

101
00:07:36,750 --> 00:07:39,340
you cannot let that stand. He must pay.

102
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:41,460
I'll lock him in a cell until he rots--

103
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:45,170
No, he has to pay the iron price.

104
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,700
They'll never respect you while he lives.

105
00:08:05,990 --> 00:08:07,570
Ser Rodrik,

106
00:08:07,690 --> 00:08:09,680
I sentence you to death.

107
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:11,960
No! You said no harm would come to them if I yielded.

108
00:08:11,970 --> 00:08:14,330
The old man couldn't keep his mouth shut.

109
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:17,420
I urge you not to make a hasty decision.

110
00:08:18,010 --> 00:08:19,860
He disrespected me in front of my men.

111
00:08:19,860 --> 00:08:21,640
That was his decision, not mine.

112
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:24,330
He is worth more to you alive than dead.

113
00:08:24,350 --> 00:08:26,370
The Starks will pay.

114
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:30,220
Please, Theon,

115
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:32,180
think what you do.

116
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:44,490
You'll address me as Prince Theon

117
00:08:44,490 --> 00:08:46,340
or you'll be next.

118
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:48,040
Come.

119
00:08:49,290 --> 00:08:50,500
No!

120
00:08:50,970 --> 00:08:53,610
- No! - Theon!

121
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:56,330
Please!

122
00:08:57,350 --> 00:08:58,680
Ser Rodrik!

123
00:08:59,530 --> 00:09:02,290
He who passes the sentence should swing the sword.

124
00:09:02,290 --> 00:09:04,310
- I'm begging you! - Coward.

125
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:09,420
Stop! Stop right now!

126
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,940
You don't give commands anymore, little Lord.

127
00:09:12,940 --> 00:09:15,930
- Please, stop this. Please stop him. - Hush now, child.

128
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:17,820
I'm off to see your father.

129
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:22,610
You said no harm would come!

130
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:26,010
You said no harm would come. Theon, please.

131
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:27,900
Any last words, old man?

132
00:09:29,030 --> 00:09:31,650
Gods help you, Theon Greyjoy.

133
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:34,250
Now you are truly lost.

134
00:09:34,880 --> 00:09:36,220
Theon, please, don't.

135
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:39,510
- Do something. - I'll do anything. Please!

136
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:41,160
No, please, stop it!

137
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:14,860
Ghost, stay with us.

138
00:10:15,550 --> 00:10:16,820
Ghost!

139
00:10:17,110 --> 00:10:18,830
There goes your pet.

140
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:20,740
He's not a pet.

141
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:22,530
You're right, he's not.

142
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:25,270
You can't tame a wild thing.

143
00:10:25,450 --> 00:10:27,280
You can't trust a wild thing.

144
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:30,000
- Ghost is different. - So you think.

145
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:32,690
Wild creatures have their own rules,

146
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,800
their own reasons.

147
00:10:34,970 --> 00:10:36,570
And you'll never know them.

148
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,490
Now the wildlings we're looking for

149
00:10:40,730 --> 00:10:43,280
sleep during the day and hunt at night.

150
00:10:45,710 --> 00:10:48,070
I thought you said you couldn't know wild things.

151
00:10:48,070 --> 00:10:49,690
I said you can't.

152
00:10:50,030 --> 00:10:53,060
They find a nice cave to hide in while the sun's up

153
00:10:53,130 --> 00:10:55,020
and do their killing when it's dark.

154
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:58,550
- We could do the same. - No, we couldn't.

155
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,360
This is their country.

156
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:03,090
They know where to walk, where not to walk.

157
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:05,390
I've lost good men who fell into a crevasse

158
00:11:05,390 --> 00:11:07,160
they didn't see till they were in it.

159
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:11,170
My father always said I'm of the north.

160
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:16,160
- I wasn't joking. - Look around, boy.

161
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:18,850
This look like home to you?

162
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:22,120
You start thinking you know this place, it'll kill you.

163
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:25,130
You understand me?

164
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:27,640
No, you don't.

165
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:29,960
We're at war.

166
00:11:30,830 --> 00:11:31,990
We've always been at war.

167
00:11:31,990 --> 00:11:34,570
It's never going to end 'cause we're not fighting an enemy.

168
00:11:34,570 --> 00:11:37,440
We're fighting the north and it's not going anywhere.

169
00:11:38,340 --> 00:11:40,880
The Watch has given you a great gift.

170
00:11:41,250 --> 00:11:43,710
You only have one thing to give in return...

171
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,190
your life.

172
00:11:45,190 --> 00:11:46,460
I'll gladly give my life.

173
00:11:46,460 --> 00:11:48,660
I don't want you to be glad about it.

174
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:50,860
I want you to curse and fight

175
00:11:50,870 --> 00:11:53,300
until your heart's done pumping.

176
00:11:53,430 --> 00:11:55,290
And know this, boy...

177
00:11:55,930 --> 00:11:59,360
Your death will be a gift for them south of the wall.

178
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,830
They'll never know what you've done.

179
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:03,070
They'll never know how you died.

180
00:12:03,070 --> 00:12:05,020
They won't even know your damn name,

181
00:12:05,570 --> 00:12:07,620
but they'll be alive because

182
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:09,700
some nameless bastard north of the wall

183
00:12:09,710 --> 00:12:11,150
gave his life for theirs.

184
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:15,200
Now, do you understand me?

185
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:17,170
I do.

186
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,760
You're even dumber than you look.

187
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,700
It's just words, boy,

188
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:25,030
to keep us a little warmer in the night,

189
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:27,450
make us feel like we've got a purpose.

190
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,160
Come on.

191
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:31,800
We've got to find these goat fuckers

192
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:33,910
before night falls and they find us.

193
00:12:46,050 --> 00:12:48,840
- Can you read? - My Lord?

194
00:12:49,650 --> 00:12:51,940
Can you read?

195
00:12:55,350 --> 00:12:57,840
This letter detailing our infantry movements

196
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:00,890
was meant for Lord Damon of House Marbrand.

197
00:13:01,210 --> 00:13:04,540
It was sent to Lord Marlyn of House Dormand.

198
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:06,180
My apologies, my lord. I must have...

199
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:09,740
Girl, fetch me the "History of the Greater and the Lesser Houses."

200
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:11,250
It's the one on the...

201
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:18,540
My cupbearer can read better than you.

202
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:31,280
To whom does House Dormand owe allegiance?

203
00:13:33,410 --> 00:13:35,320
My Lord, I...

204
00:13:35,320 --> 00:13:38,080
To the Starks of Winterfell!

205
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:42,350
Who have 20,000 men and my son!

206
00:13:43,940 --> 00:13:46,020
I judged you might be good for something more

207
00:13:46,020 --> 00:13:48,280
than brutalizing peasants.

208
00:13:48,690 --> 00:13:51,070
I see I overestimated you.

209
00:13:52,170 --> 00:13:55,610
If you ever put my son's life at risk again, I'll...

210
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:58,600
Leave us.

211
00:14:06,330 --> 00:14:08,220
Put the book away, girl.

212
00:14:14,970 --> 00:14:18,540
Maybe you should devise our next battle plan while you're about it.

213
00:14:23,990 --> 00:14:26,130
Lord Petyr Baelish.

214
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:29,280
Give us the room.

215
00:14:37,540 --> 00:14:39,150
Clear all this.

216
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:45,470
- Lord Tywin. - Baelish.

217
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,580
- Wine? - Thank you.

218
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:00,680
What news from the capital?

219
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:04,170
I travelled here directly from Renly Baratheon's camp.

220
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:06,630
Ah, the late king Renly.

221
00:15:06,940 --> 00:15:08,760
Rather a short reign.

222
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:10,690
Murdered by a woman, I hear.

223
00:15:10,690 --> 00:15:12,320
So they say.

224
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:17,820
There has been talk of other forces at work,

225
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:20,360
dark forces.

226
00:15:21,520 --> 00:15:22,610
Here.

227
00:15:25,620 --> 00:15:29,870
Men love to blame demons when their grand plans unravel.

228
00:15:31,060 --> 00:15:33,530
It is my belief that a moment of chaos

229
00:15:33,530 --> 00:15:36,820
affords opportunities lost soon after.

230
00:15:36,820 --> 00:15:40,060
You say that as if you were the first man alive to think it.

231
00:15:40,060 --> 00:15:42,410
Yes, a crisis is an opportunity.

232
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:45,170
What other brilliant insights have you brought me today?

233
00:15:45,170 --> 00:15:46,800
After the Lannisters and the Starks,

234
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:49,260
the Tyrells command the largest host.

235
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:51,300
Their lands are the most fertile in the Seven Kingdoms,

236
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:55,430
- feeding horses and soldiers... - Yes, yes, yes.

237
00:15:55,430 --> 00:15:59,210
The Tyrells have not yet declared for any of the surviving kings.

238
00:15:59,890 --> 00:16:01,000
Loras wants revenge.

239
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,390
He blames Stannis for Renly's death.

240
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:05,640
And Margaery...

241
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,730
Wants to be queen.

242
00:16:08,130 --> 00:16:10,270
Yes, she does.

243
00:16:11,870 --> 00:16:15,180
House Tyrell rebelled against the Iron Throne,

244
00:16:15,650 --> 00:16:18,910
- against my grandson. - They did.

245
00:16:19,330 --> 00:16:21,900
And perhaps that treason should be punished

246
00:16:21,970 --> 00:16:23,390
one day,

247
00:16:23,620 --> 00:16:27,480
after Stannis and Robb Stark are defeated.

248
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,990
More wine for Lord Baelish.

249
00:16:38,010 --> 00:16:41,420
If you will allow me to represent your family's interests,

250
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:43,650
I believe that an advantageous agreement...

251
00:16:43,650 --> 00:16:46,480
The Tyrell host has returned to Highgarden?

252
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,840
They have.

253
00:16:49,130 --> 00:16:50,640
Pardon, My Lord.

254
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,500
It's only wine.

255
00:16:53,870 --> 00:16:55,910
You would ride there yourself?

256
00:16:56,090 --> 00:16:58,320
Tonight, with your leave.

257
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,830
I'll have an answer by nightfall.

258
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:01,530
That'll be all, girl.

259
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:08,980
What else?

260
00:17:09,210 --> 00:17:11,260
On your son Tyrion's directive,

261
00:17:11,260 --> 00:17:13,950
I met with Catelyn Stark.

262
00:17:14,010 --> 00:17:15,160
Why?

263
00:17:15,390 --> 00:17:17,980
He had an interesting proposal for her

264
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:20,310
concerning her daughters.

265
00:18:10,690 --> 00:18:13,100
- A girl. - A wildling.

266
00:18:14,700 --> 00:18:16,120
We could question her.

267
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:17,640
You could.

268
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:19,810
She won't answer.

269
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:23,260
I've known a wildling to bite off his tongue instead of talking.

270
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:27,440
- What's your name? - Ygritte.

271
00:18:27,450 --> 00:18:30,010
She was reaching for this axe when you got to her.

272
00:18:30,510 --> 00:18:33,420
Give her half a chance, she'll bury it in your face.

273
00:18:34,560 --> 00:18:36,260
I gave you my name.

274
00:18:38,140 --> 00:18:39,680
I'm Jon Snow.

275
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:49,750
You ought to burn them you killed.

276
00:18:49,750 --> 00:18:51,520
We'd need a big fire for that.

277
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:55,590
Tell me, Ygritte,

278
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:58,390
Why do you want us to build a big fire?

279
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,950
Are there some more friends in the area?

280
00:19:01,450 --> 00:19:04,930
Burn them or maybe you'll need those swords again.

281
00:19:05,070 --> 00:19:07,400
Our boy here's already killed one dead man.

282
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:09,180
He can do it again if he has to.

283
00:19:10,210 --> 00:19:12,160
What waits beyond the pass?

284
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,700
- The free folk. - How many?

285
00:19:16,450 --> 00:19:18,550
Hundreds and thousands.

286
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:21,070
More than you've ever seen, crow.

287
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:23,730
Why come to the mountains?

288
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:27,170
What's in the Frostfangs your king could want?

289
00:19:35,170 --> 00:19:36,950
Do you mean to march on the Wall?

290
00:19:43,460 --> 00:19:45,600
Do you know who I am, girl?

291
00:19:45,970 --> 00:19:47,720
Qhorin Halfhand.

292
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:49,780
Tell me true.

293
00:19:50,830 --> 00:19:52,700
If your people captured me,

294
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:55,160
would they take me prisoner?

295
00:19:55,250 --> 00:19:59,030
They'd take your head off your shoulders if they was feeling kind.

296
00:19:59,330 --> 00:20:01,950
If not, they'd kill you slow.

297
00:20:05,020 --> 00:20:06,670
We have no food for her.

298
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:09,020
Can't spare a man to watch her.

299
00:20:09,410 --> 00:20:10,040
Can't let her go.

300
00:20:10,040 --> 00:20:12,550
She'll bring Mance Rayder's army down on us.

301
00:20:13,010 --> 00:20:14,320
It needs to be done.

302
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:15,840
- Want me to do it? - No.

303
00:20:17,790 --> 00:20:19,310
No, I'll do it.

304
00:20:21,330 --> 00:20:22,730
Come, brothers.

305
00:20:23,190 --> 00:20:24,720
We'll leave him to it.

306
00:20:25,310 --> 00:20:26,960
We'll meet you at the top.

307
00:20:27,030 --> 00:20:28,550
Don't take too long.

308
00:20:28,850 --> 00:20:30,930
We're deep in their country now.

309
00:20:43,830 --> 00:20:46,330
You never killed a woman before, did you?

310
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,920
You don't need to do it.

311
00:20:50,150 --> 00:20:52,480
Mance would take you. I know he would.

312
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:54,750
There's secret ways.

313
00:20:54,750 --> 00:20:56,310
The crows would never catch us.

314
00:20:58,190 --> 00:21:00,410
I'm as much a crow as they are.

315
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:16,100
Will you burn me... after?

316
00:21:17,290 --> 00:21:18,420
Can't.

317
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:21,740
Someone might see the smoke.

318
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:29,670
Strike hard and true,

319
00:21:29,900 --> 00:21:31,720
Jon Snow,

320
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:34,690
or I'll come back and haunt you.

321
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:40,180
That's cold.

322
00:21:43,490 --> 00:21:44,800
Go on.

323
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:46,740
Be quick about it.

324
00:21:54,630 --> 00:21:55,970
Do it.

325
00:21:59,120 --> 00:22:01,320
Bastard, do it!

326
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:20,000
You can't do it. We both know it.

327
00:23:25,260 --> 00:23:27,430
The sun's going down, Jon Snow.

328
00:23:27,690 --> 00:23:30,020
And your friends are nowhere close.

329
00:23:30,310 --> 00:23:31,880
I'll find them.

330
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:35,180
Call for them. Go on.

331
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:37,180
Call loudly.

332
00:23:44,520 --> 00:23:47,920
May the Seven guide the princess on her journey.

333
00:23:48,170 --> 00:23:50,390
May the Mother give her health.

334
00:23:50,390 --> 00:23:52,890
May the Crone give her wisdom.

335
00:23:52,970 --> 00:23:55,950
May the Warrior give her courage.

336
00:24:00,830 --> 00:24:03,010
One day I pray you love someone.

337
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:06,330
I pray you love her so much,

338
00:24:06,600 --> 00:24:08,990
when you close your eyes, you see her face.

339
00:24:11,150 --> 00:24:12,780
I want that for you.

340
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:16,910
I want you to know what it's like to love someone,

341
00:24:17,760 --> 00:24:19,850
to truly love someone,

342
00:24:21,230 --> 00:24:23,280
before I take her from you.

343
00:24:40,660 --> 00:24:43,330
You sound like a little cat mewling for his mother.

344
00:24:43,510 --> 00:24:45,100
Princes don't cry.

345
00:24:45,100 --> 00:24:48,480
- I saw you cry. - Did you say something, My Lady?

346
00:24:48,480 --> 00:24:51,190
My little brother cried when I left Winterfell.

347
00:24:51,190 --> 00:24:52,390
So?

348
00:24:52,790 --> 00:24:54,800
It seems a normal thing.

349
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:57,030
Is your little brother a prince?

350
00:24:57,030 --> 00:24:58,120
No.

351
00:24:58,850 --> 00:25:00,910
Not really relevant, then, is it?

352
00:25:04,690 --> 00:25:06,150
Come, Dog.

353
00:25:14,540 --> 00:25:16,570
Hail, Joffrey!

354
00:25:16,570 --> 00:25:18,660
Hail to the king.

355
00:25:20,850 --> 00:25:23,130
Seven blessings on you, Your Grace.

356
00:25:23,130 --> 00:25:25,180
Murderer! Bastard!

357
00:25:25,180 --> 00:25:26,760
All hail the king.

358
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:29,200
He's no king. He's a bastard!

359
00:25:30,250 --> 00:25:32,500
Please, Your Grace, we're hungry.

360
00:25:34,910 --> 00:25:38,200
- Freak! - Get the prince back to the keep now.

361
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:40,180
Yes, My Lord. Come, quickly.

362
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:42,620
Please, Your Grace, give us some food!

363
00:25:42,620 --> 00:25:45,070
Bread, Your Grace, please!

364
00:25:48,070 --> 00:25:49,530
Who threw that?

365
00:25:50,370 --> 00:25:52,090
I want the man who threw that.

366
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:53,970
Find who did that and bring him to me!

367
00:25:53,970 --> 00:25:55,980
- Hold on! - Hold them back!

368
00:25:56,010 --> 00:25:58,260
Just kill them! Kill them all!

369
00:26:03,550 --> 00:26:06,200
- Move. Move! - Pull back!

370
00:26:06,550 --> 00:26:07,900
Tear him to pieces!

371
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:10,840
What are you doing? I want these people executed!

372
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:12,620
And they want the same for you.

373
00:26:40,300 --> 00:26:41,740
Where's Sansa?

374
00:26:44,660 --> 00:26:45,790
Through the door!

375
00:26:46,020 --> 00:26:47,110
Come on!

376
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:54,270
Protect the king!

377
00:26:54,560 --> 00:26:56,870
- Get back! - Fall back!

378
00:26:56,880 --> 00:26:59,260
- Move! - To the gates!

379
00:27:10,930 --> 00:27:14,460
- Come in! Come in! - Keep him safe!

380
00:27:14,460 --> 00:27:16,130
Motherfucker!

381
00:27:17,030 --> 00:27:19,480
- Watch out. Hold them back. - Come on.

382
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:31,100
Traitors!

383
00:27:31,700 --> 00:27:32,970
I'll have all their heads.

384
00:27:32,980 --> 00:27:35,000
Oh, you blind, bloody fool.

385
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:36,810
You can't insult me.

386
00:27:36,820 --> 00:27:40,040
We've had vicious kings and we've had idiot kings,

387
00:27:40,040 --> 00:27:41,450
but I don't know if we've ever been cursed

388
00:27:41,450 --> 00:27:42,710
with a vicious idiot for a king.

389
00:27:42,710 --> 00:27:44,350
- You can't... - I can, I am.

390
00:27:44,350 --> 00:27:45,930
They attacked me!

391
00:27:45,930 --> 00:27:49,520
They threw a cow pie at you, so you decided to kill them all?

392
00:27:49,520 --> 00:27:51,330
They're starving, you fool.

393
00:27:51,330 --> 00:27:53,010
All because of a war you started.

394
00:27:53,010 --> 00:27:55,180
You're talking to a king!

395
00:27:55,680 --> 00:27:57,650
And now I've struck a king.

396
00:27:57,650 --> 00:27:59,760
Did my hand fall from my wrist?

397
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:02,290
Where is the Stark girl?

398
00:28:02,290 --> 00:28:03,560
Let them have her.

399
00:28:03,570 --> 00:28:06,890
If she dies, you'll never get your uncle Jaime back.

400
00:28:07,350 --> 00:28:09,640
You owe him quite a bit, you know.

401
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:19,910
Where are you going?

402
00:28:22,190 --> 00:28:24,760
You ever been fucked, little girl?

403
00:28:25,600 --> 00:28:26,520
Come here.

404
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,590
Take some men and go and find the Stark girl.

405
00:28:29,590 --> 00:28:31,590
I take my orders from the king.

406
00:28:33,020 --> 00:28:33,820
This way!

407
00:28:41,930 --> 00:28:42,680
Please!

408
00:28:43,790 --> 00:28:45,010
No, no.

409
00:29:04,380 --> 00:29:05,310
Please!

410
00:29:09,370 --> 00:29:10,710
You're all right now, little bird.

411
00:29:10,710 --> 00:29:11,850
You're all right.

412
00:29:27,270 --> 00:29:28,070
We'll get you. We'll get you.

413
00:29:28,960 --> 00:29:30,000
This way.

414
00:29:32,670 --> 00:29:33,810
Are you hurt, My Lady?

415
00:29:34,310 --> 00:29:35,580
The little bird's bleeding.

416
00:29:35,580 --> 00:29:37,380
Someone take her back to her cage,

417
00:29:37,380 --> 00:29:38,630
see to that cut.

418
00:29:38,630 --> 00:29:39,800
Well done, Clegane.

419
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:43,160
I didn't do it for you.

420
00:29:45,610 --> 00:29:47,220
He shouldn't make me wait.

421
00:29:47,870 --> 00:29:51,350
The Spice King is the second wealthiest man in Qarth.

422
00:29:52,040 --> 00:29:53,660
He makes everyone wait.

423
00:29:54,290 --> 00:29:57,270
Of course, you could have avoided this embarrassment

424
00:29:57,270 --> 00:29:59,940
if you married the wealthiest man in Qarth.

425
00:29:59,940 --> 00:30:01,790
I already have a husband.

426
00:30:01,790 --> 00:30:03,970
Khal Drogo is gone, Khaleesi.

427
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:07,140
You are far too young to be a widow forever.

428
00:30:07,620 --> 00:30:10,570
And far too beautiful.

429
00:30:10,570 --> 00:30:12,130
And you are far too smart

430
00:30:12,130 --> 00:30:14,490
to think that I will succumb to flattery.

431
00:30:15,390 --> 00:30:17,610
I have travelled very far in my life

432
00:30:17,610 --> 00:30:18,910
and met many women,

433
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:21,390
but none that are immune to flattery.

434
00:30:21,570 --> 00:30:24,100
The Mother of Dragons!

435
00:30:24,100 --> 00:30:25,520
Here he comes.

436
00:30:26,050 --> 00:30:29,560
Forgive me. I had terrible dreams last night.

437
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:31,440
Terrible dreams.

438
00:30:31,890 --> 00:30:34,520
I could not sleep until the sun was shining

439
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:36,270
and the birds were singing.

440
00:30:37,390 --> 00:30:39,830
Look what a beauty you are

441
00:30:39,830 --> 00:30:42,670
now the Red Waste has been washed off you.

442
00:30:42,870 --> 00:30:46,450
I am sorry about all that unpleasantness.

443
00:30:46,450 --> 00:30:50,640
The silver hair of a true Targaryen.

444
00:30:50,640 --> 00:30:53,880
Xaro Xhoan Daxos, she is far too lovely

445
00:30:53,880 --> 00:30:56,440
for a glorified dockworker like yourself.

446
00:30:56,440 --> 00:30:59,860
Very true, and yet they say that your grandfather,

447
00:30:59,860 --> 00:31:02,050
who sold pepper off the back of a wagon,

448
00:31:02,050 --> 00:31:05,560
married a lady far lovelier and higher born than himself.

449
00:31:05,560 --> 00:31:07,920
Every lady alive was lovelier

450
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:10,440
and higher born than my grandfather.

451
00:31:12,190 --> 00:31:15,620
Did my servants not offer you something to eat, to drink?

452
00:31:15,860 --> 00:31:17,080
I'll have them flogged in the square.

453
00:31:17,080 --> 00:31:19,460
Thank you, my lord. You are a gracious host,

454
00:31:19,460 --> 00:31:22,260
but there is no servant alive that can bring me what I want.

455
00:31:22,580 --> 00:31:25,090
Oh, she has a talent for drama, this one.

456
00:31:25,500 --> 00:31:29,340
So, my little princess, what is it you want?

457
00:31:29,340 --> 00:31:30,690
My birthright...

458
00:31:30,690 --> 00:31:32,830
the Seven Kingdoms of Westeros.

459
00:31:33,020 --> 00:31:35,520
I fear I'm no better than a servant in this regard.

460
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:37,620
I cannot give you what I do not have.

461
00:31:37,620 --> 00:31:40,280
I'm not asking you for the kingdoms.

462
00:31:40,280 --> 00:31:42,040
I'm asking you for ships.

463
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:43,550
I need to cross the Narrow Sea.

464
00:31:43,550 --> 00:31:45,190
I need my ships as well.

465
00:31:45,390 --> 00:31:48,960
I use them, you see, to bring spices from one port to another.

466
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:50,890
Whatever you grant me now will be repaid

467
00:31:50,890 --> 00:31:53,700
three times over when I retake the Iron Throne.

468
00:31:53,700 --> 00:31:54,780
Retake?

469
00:31:55,370 --> 00:31:57,500
Did you once sit on the Iron Throne?

470
00:31:57,500 --> 00:32:00,460
My father sat there before he was murdered.

471
00:32:00,890 --> 00:32:02,690
But if you did not sit on it yourself,

472
00:32:02,690 --> 00:32:06,300
would it not be correct to say take the Iron Throne?

473
00:32:06,390 --> 00:32:08,400
I didn't come here to argue grammar.

474
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:11,110
Of course not. You came to take my ships.

475
00:32:11,940 --> 00:32:15,070
So let me explain my position, little princess.

476
00:32:16,010 --> 00:32:19,380
Unlike you, I do not have exalted ancestors.

477
00:32:19,380 --> 00:32:21,200
I make my living by trade.

478
00:32:21,200 --> 00:32:24,500
And I judge every trade on its merits.

479
00:32:24,500 --> 00:32:26,300
You ask for ships.

480
00:32:26,300 --> 00:32:29,400
You say I shall be repaid triple.

481
00:32:29,800 --> 00:32:32,680
I do not doubt your honesty or your intentions.

482
00:32:32,680 --> 00:32:34,480
But before you repay your debts,

483
00:32:34,480 --> 00:32:37,180
you must seize the Seven Kingdoms.

484
00:32:37,460 --> 00:32:38,740
Do you have an army?

485
00:32:38,740 --> 00:32:39,410
Not yet.

486
00:32:39,410 --> 00:32:40,990
You do not have an army.

487
00:32:41,410 --> 00:32:43,810
Do you have powerful allies in Westeros?

488
00:32:43,810 --> 00:32:45,700
There are many there that support my claim.

489
00:32:45,700 --> 00:32:47,390
When were you there last?

490
00:32:48,170 --> 00:32:49,900
I left when I was a baby.

491
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:52,780
So, in truth, you have no allies.

492
00:32:52,780 --> 00:32:57,320
The people will rise to fight for their rightful queen when I return.

493
00:32:59,410 --> 00:33:00,730
Forgive me, little princess,

494
00:33:00,730 --> 00:33:04,450
but I cannot make an investment based on wishes and dreams.

495
00:33:04,790 --> 00:33:05,880
Now if you'll pardon me.

496
00:33:05,880 --> 00:33:08,760
Do you know Illyrio Mopatis, Magister of Pentos?

497
00:33:09,080 --> 00:33:11,380
Yes, we've met. A shrewd man.

498
00:33:11,380 --> 00:33:14,620
For my wedding he gave me three petrified dragon eggs.

499
00:33:14,620 --> 00:33:17,710
He believed-- the world believed...

500
00:33:17,710 --> 00:33:19,620
that the ages had turned them to stone.

501
00:33:19,620 --> 00:33:22,940
How many centuries has it been since dragons roamed the skies?

502
00:33:22,940 --> 00:33:25,920
But I dreamt that if I carried those eggs

503
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:28,570
into a great fire, they would hatch.

504
00:33:28,820 --> 00:33:33,110
When I stepped into the fire, my own people thought I was mad.

505
00:33:33,110 --> 00:33:35,090
But when the fire burned out,

506
00:33:35,650 --> 00:33:36,940
I was unhurt,

507
00:33:37,500 --> 00:33:39,490
the Mother of Dragons.

508
00:33:43,030 --> 00:33:44,730
Do you understand?

509
00:33:47,870 --> 00:33:49,720
I'm no ordinary woman.

510
00:33:50,600 --> 00:33:52,800
My dreams come true.

511
00:33:58,120 --> 00:34:00,310
I admire your passion.

512
00:34:01,840 --> 00:34:04,850
But in business, I trust in logic, not passion.

513
00:34:05,260 --> 00:34:07,170
I'm sorry, little princess.

514
00:34:07,170 --> 00:34:09,400
I am not your little princess.

515
00:34:09,610 --> 00:34:10,970
I am Daenerys Stormborn

516
00:34:10,970 --> 00:34:12,610
of the blood of old Valyria

517
00:34:12,610 --> 00:34:14,560
and I will take what is mine

518
00:34:14,560 --> 00:34:17,240
with fire and blood, I will take it.

519
00:34:17,240 --> 00:34:21,110
Yes, My Lady, but not with my ships.

520
00:34:39,500 --> 00:34:40,980
Who taught you to read?

521
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:44,160
My father, My Lord.

522
00:34:46,640 --> 00:34:48,310
I taught my son Jaime to read.

523
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:53,160
The Maester came to me one day,

524
00:34:53,160 --> 00:34:54,560
told me he wasn't learning.

525
00:34:55,750 --> 00:34:57,440
He couldn't make sense of the letters.

526
00:34:58,400 --> 00:35:00,090
He reversed them in his head.

527
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:03,490
The Maester said he'd heard tell of this affliction

528
00:35:04,390 --> 00:35:06,210
and that we simply must accept it.

529
00:35:09,070 --> 00:35:11,720
After that, I sat Jaime down

530
00:35:11,720 --> 00:35:14,840
for four hours every day until he learned.

531
00:35:16,060 --> 00:35:18,690
He hated me for it, for a time.

532
00:35:20,100 --> 00:35:21,480
For a long time,

533
00:35:22,840 --> 00:35:23,990
but he learned.

534
00:35:29,470 --> 00:35:32,260
Where is your father? Is he alive?

535
00:35:35,510 --> 00:35:36,850
Who was he?

536
00:35:37,330 --> 00:35:39,500
A stonemason.

537
00:35:40,250 --> 00:35:42,970
A stonemason who could read?

538
00:35:42,970 --> 00:35:44,780
He taught himself.

539
00:35:45,390 --> 00:35:46,440
Quite a man.

540
00:35:48,260 --> 00:35:49,400
What killed him?

541
00:35:52,070 --> 00:35:53,560
Loyalty.

542
00:35:55,740 --> 00:35:57,960
You're a sharp little thing, aren't you?

543
00:36:01,350 --> 00:36:02,170
Did...

544
00:36:04,590 --> 00:36:06,930
Forgive me, My Lord. I shouldn't ask questions.

545
00:36:08,650 --> 00:36:09,710
No...

546
00:36:11,120 --> 00:36:12,770
but you've already begun.

547
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:17,010
Did you know your father, My Lord?

548
00:36:18,570 --> 00:36:19,760
I did.

549
00:36:21,530 --> 00:36:22,720
I grew up with him.

550
00:36:25,440 --> 00:36:27,540
I watched him grow old.

551
00:36:31,390 --> 00:36:32,620
He loved us.

552
00:36:33,190 --> 00:36:34,640
He was a good man,

553
00:36:36,370 --> 00:36:37,860
but a weak man,

554
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:41,640
a weak man who nearly destroyed our house and name.

555
00:36:44,640 --> 00:36:45,860
I'm cold.

556
00:36:46,880 --> 00:36:48,990
I'll fetch more wood for the fire, My Lord.

557
00:37:17,990 --> 00:37:19,270
Where are you going, girl?

558
00:37:20,470 --> 00:37:22,400
The armory, My Lord.

559
00:37:23,370 --> 00:37:24,130
Why?

560
00:37:24,600 --> 00:37:25,710
Lord Tywin sent me.

561
00:37:28,420 --> 00:37:29,590
What might this be?

562
00:37:30,950 --> 00:37:32,430
Lord Tywin gave it to me.

563
00:37:34,050 --> 00:37:34,880
What for?

564
00:37:35,880 --> 00:37:37,380
To take to the armory.

565
00:37:39,100 --> 00:37:40,650
Why would he do that?

566
00:37:43,290 --> 00:37:44,630
Let's go and ask him.

567
00:37:47,080 --> 00:37:47,920
Move!

568
00:37:50,770 --> 00:37:52,350
Get out of the way!

569
00:38:23,130 --> 00:38:24,380
Amory Lorch.

570
00:38:25,350 --> 00:38:27,140
A girl has named a second name.

571
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:28,740
A man will do what must be done.

572
00:38:28,740 --> 00:38:29,780
Now!

573
00:38:31,130 --> 00:38:33,850
A girl cannot tell a man when exactly he must do a thing.

574
00:38:34,670 --> 00:38:36,880
A man cannot make a thing happen before its time.

575
00:38:36,880 --> 00:38:38,690
But he's going to tell Tywin. He's getting away.

576
00:38:38,690 --> 00:38:40,090
It has to be now.

577
00:38:48,950 --> 00:38:49,990
Guard!

578
00:39:00,580 --> 00:39:03,360
- Your Grace. - Your Grace.

579
00:39:07,370 --> 00:39:08,710
My honor, Your Grace.

580
00:39:09,450 --> 00:39:10,350
Your Grace.

581
00:39:17,190 --> 00:39:18,390
- Your Grace. - Quent.

582
00:39:40,610 --> 00:39:41,690
Lady Talisa.

583
00:39:43,670 --> 00:39:44,650
Your Grace.

584
00:39:46,500 --> 00:39:48,180
I'm not sure I'm a lady.

585
00:39:48,180 --> 00:39:50,620
Westerosi customs are still a bit foreign to me.

586
00:39:50,790 --> 00:39:52,890
It's hard to keep all the rules straight.

587
00:39:52,890 --> 00:39:55,670
But if I remember my lessons,

588
00:39:56,040 --> 00:39:58,400
a woman of noble birth is always called a lady

589
00:39:58,960 --> 00:40:01,440
unless she's a queen or a princess.

590
00:40:01,630 --> 00:40:03,040
I could find someone who knows.

591
00:40:03,460 --> 00:40:05,430
Why are you so sure I'm of noble birth?

592
00:40:06,330 --> 00:40:07,610
Because it's obvious.

593
00:40:08,950 --> 00:40:11,690
What if I told you my father sold lace on the long bridge

594
00:40:11,690 --> 00:40:14,460
and my mother, my brother, and I lived with him above our shop?

595
00:40:16,310 --> 00:40:17,650
I'd call you a liar.

596
00:40:17,910 --> 00:40:20,940
Not very noble to accuse a lady of dishonesty.

597
00:40:25,260 --> 00:40:27,070
I always thought I was a brilliant liar.

598
00:40:27,970 --> 00:40:29,880
Better at amputations, I'm afraid.

599
00:40:35,630 --> 00:40:37,070
Quite a pretty spot.

600
00:40:37,650 --> 00:40:38,810
Will we be here long?

601
00:40:39,910 --> 00:40:42,250
I couldn't really discuss troop movements with you.

602
00:40:43,810 --> 00:40:44,940
I'm not a spy.

603
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:48,300
Of course a spy would deny being a spy.

604
00:40:49,280 --> 00:40:52,110
You're right. You've found me out.

605
00:40:52,110 --> 00:40:53,650
I'm writing a letter to the Lannisters.

606
00:40:53,650 --> 00:40:56,080
"The young wolf is on the move."

607
00:40:58,190 --> 00:40:59,560
Perhaps you'd join me...

608
00:41:01,360 --> 00:41:04,150
If you've got time, of course, for, well...

609
00:41:04,150 --> 00:41:05,040
Robb.

610
00:41:07,790 --> 00:41:08,680
Mother.

611
00:41:15,750 --> 00:41:18,360
Mother, this is Lady Talisa.

612
00:41:19,100 --> 00:41:20,870
She's been helping with the wounded.

613
00:41:20,870 --> 00:41:23,790
She's been very... helpful.

614
00:41:24,410 --> 00:41:25,400
Lady Talisa.

615
00:41:25,400 --> 00:41:26,640
Lady stark.

616
00:41:27,500 --> 00:41:29,020
Lady Talisa...?

617
00:41:29,580 --> 00:41:30,400
Maegyr.

618
00:41:30,590 --> 00:41:31,680
Maegyr?

619
00:41:32,580 --> 00:41:35,460
Forgive me, I do not know this name.

620
00:41:35,570 --> 00:41:38,510
An uncommon name here. An old name in Volantis.

621
00:41:39,410 --> 00:41:41,820
Excuse me, My Lady. Your Grace.

622
00:41:51,410 --> 00:41:52,470
I've missed you.

623
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:56,510
Yes, you look positively forlorn.

624
00:41:56,660 --> 00:41:58,740
You surprised me, that's all.

625
00:41:59,890 --> 00:42:01,200
I didn't think I'd see you today.

626
00:42:02,650 --> 00:42:04,980
I wish that you were free to follow your heart.

627
00:42:04,980 --> 00:42:05,800
I know.

628
00:42:06,390 --> 00:42:09,270
You have inherited your father's responsibilities.

629
00:42:10,260 --> 00:42:11,940
I'm afraid they come at a cost.

630
00:42:12,010 --> 00:42:15,280
- You are promised to another. - I know.

631
00:42:16,360 --> 00:42:18,770
A debt that must be paid.

632
00:42:19,930 --> 00:42:21,940
- I haven't forgotten. - Your Grace.

633
00:42:22,430 --> 00:42:25,280
My Lady. News from Winterfell.

634
00:42:38,420 --> 00:42:40,230
Your brothers desert you?

635
00:42:41,590 --> 00:42:43,440
I can tell you which way to go.

636
00:42:44,820 --> 00:42:45,990
We'll stop here.

637
00:42:46,520 --> 00:42:48,490
Too dark to go any farther today.

638
00:42:48,490 --> 00:42:51,230
Here? There's no shelter here.

639
00:42:51,230 --> 00:42:52,580
There's no shelter anywhere.

640
00:42:52,580 --> 00:42:55,610
There is if you know where to look.

641
00:42:58,760 --> 00:43:00,570
The cold could kill us both.

642
00:43:00,570 --> 00:43:02,670
- If you light a fire... - No fire.

643
00:43:03,090 --> 00:43:04,940
- But a fire is... - No fire.

644
00:43:08,130 --> 00:43:09,470
Have it your way.

645
00:43:17,290 --> 00:43:19,600
We'll stay warmer if we stay close.

646
00:43:22,090 --> 00:43:24,580
Bet you freeze to death before I do.

647
00:43:25,810 --> 00:43:27,360
Bet your life.

648
00:43:53,190 --> 00:43:54,710
Think they're out looking for you?

649
00:43:56,630 --> 00:43:59,010
- Yes. - Think they'll find you?

650
00:44:00,530 --> 00:44:01,380
Yes.

651
00:44:04,280 --> 00:44:05,830
You're brave.

652
00:44:07,420 --> 00:44:08,540
Stupid,

653
00:44:09,450 --> 00:44:10,590
but brave.

654
00:44:14,180 --> 00:44:16,790
We start again at first light. Get some sleep.

655
00:44:33,190 --> 00:44:34,250
Stop moving.

656
00:44:34,960 --> 00:44:37,000
I'm just trying to get comfortable.

657
00:44:38,470 --> 00:44:39,630
Stop it!

658
00:44:52,610 --> 00:44:54,420
- You're still moving. - Was I?

659
00:44:55,480 --> 00:44:57,370
I didn't notice that time.

660
00:45:09,140 --> 00:45:10,590
This cannot be true.

661
00:45:11,040 --> 00:45:12,630
We've had ravens from White Harbor,

662
00:45:13,110 --> 00:45:14,530
Barrowton and the Dreadfort.

663
00:45:15,140 --> 00:45:16,420
I'm afraid it is true.

664
00:45:17,590 --> 00:45:19,460
Why? Why would Theon...

665
00:45:19,460 --> 00:45:22,100
Because the Greyjoys are treasonous whores.

666
00:45:22,570 --> 00:45:24,980
- My brothers? - We've heard nothing of them.

667
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:29,020
But Rodrik Cassel is dead.

668
00:45:31,130 --> 00:45:33,860
I told you, never trust a Greyjoy!

669
00:45:36,770 --> 00:45:38,380
I must go North at once.

670
00:45:38,830 --> 00:45:40,470
There's still a war to win, Your Grace.

671
00:45:40,470 --> 00:45:43,220
How can I call myself king if I can't hold my own castle?

672
00:45:43,640 --> 00:45:46,490
- How can I ask men to follow me if I can't-- - You are a king.

673
00:45:46,830 --> 00:45:49,660
And that means you don't have to do everything yourself.

674
00:45:49,660 --> 00:45:51,290
Let me go and talk to Theon.

675
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:53,600
There will be no talk. He will die for this.

676
00:45:54,710 --> 00:45:57,440
Theon holds the castle with a skeleton crew.

677
00:45:57,620 --> 00:46:00,120
Let me send word to my bastard at the Dreadfort.

678
00:46:00,120 --> 00:46:01,420
He can raise a few hundred men

679
00:46:01,420 --> 00:46:03,870
and retake Winterfell before the new moon.

680
00:46:04,350 --> 00:46:06,530
We have the Lannisters on the run.

681
00:46:07,570 --> 00:46:09,360
If you march all the way back north now,

682
00:46:09,360 --> 00:46:11,000
you'll lose what you gained.

683
00:46:11,980 --> 00:46:15,290
My boy would be honored to bring you Prince Theon's head.

684
00:46:16,810 --> 00:46:19,340
Tell your son Bran and Rickon's safety is paramount.

685
00:46:20,480 --> 00:46:23,310
And Theon... I want him brought to me alive.

686
00:46:24,930 --> 00:46:27,050
I want to look him in the eye and ask him why.

687
00:46:27,590 --> 00:46:29,650
And then I'll take his head myself.

688
00:46:30,540 --> 00:46:31,610
Why on earth would I trust

689
00:46:31,610 --> 00:46:33,910
the word of a lying little savage like you?

690
00:46:33,910 --> 00:46:35,020
I'm no liar.

691
00:46:37,000 --> 00:46:38,780
All wildlings are liars and savages

692
00:46:38,780 --> 00:46:40,940
with no loyalty to anything or anyone.

693
00:46:40,940 --> 00:46:43,330
I done what I had to do to stay alive.

694
00:46:44,360 --> 00:46:46,540
I hate the Starks as well as you do.

695
00:46:46,540 --> 00:46:48,600
Let me serve you, My Lord.

696
00:46:49,070 --> 00:46:52,100
How? And don't tell me to put a spear in your hand.

697
00:46:52,460 --> 00:46:54,780
There are other ways to serve, My Lord.

698
00:46:55,580 --> 00:46:57,290
I'm a prince now, and you'd do well...

699
00:46:57,290 --> 00:47:00,470
There are other ways to serve, My Prince.

700
00:47:04,820 --> 00:47:05,830
Like what?

701
00:47:08,900 --> 00:47:11,670
We know things, the free people.

702
00:47:12,330 --> 00:47:13,800
You know things?

703
00:47:15,350 --> 00:47:16,460
Like what?

704
00:47:16,660 --> 00:47:17,940
How to eat dirt?

705
00:47:20,180 --> 00:47:21,360
Other things.

706
00:47:22,550 --> 00:47:24,580
Savage things.

707
00:47:27,400 --> 00:47:28,640
Wait outside.

708
00:47:46,330 --> 00:47:48,370
I always wondered what you had under there.

709
00:47:49,760 --> 00:47:51,130
It comes at a price.

710
00:47:51,800 --> 00:47:53,520
I'm not killing you. That's your price.

711
00:47:53,520 --> 00:47:54,800
I already had that.

712
00:47:57,020 --> 00:47:58,090
What do you want, then,

713
00:47:58,580 --> 00:48:00,500
other than your miserable life?

714
00:48:01,270 --> 00:48:02,900
What all free people want...

715
00:48:03,320 --> 00:48:04,440
my freedom.

716
00:48:10,260 --> 00:48:11,480
Well, you shall have it, then.

717
00:48:14,260 --> 00:48:16,570
But only if you serve me well.

718
00:48:24,770 --> 00:48:27,800
- It's not deep. - I thought they were going to kill me.

719
00:48:27,800 --> 00:48:29,460
They thought so, too.

720
00:48:29,870 --> 00:48:31,950
He hated me, the man who hit me.

721
00:48:31,950 --> 00:48:34,500
I saw it in his eyes. Hated me.

722
00:48:35,170 --> 00:48:36,440
He never met me before,

723
00:48:36,440 --> 00:48:39,210
but he wanted to hurt me.

724
00:48:39,520 --> 00:48:40,390
Of course he did.

725
00:48:40,390 --> 00:48:42,430
Why? Why would a stranger...

726
00:48:42,430 --> 00:48:44,710
You are everything he will never have.

727
00:48:44,710 --> 00:48:47,030
Your horse eats better than his children.

728
00:48:47,910 --> 00:48:49,860
It doesn't matter now. He's dead.

729
00:48:50,630 --> 00:48:52,790
I would have given them bread if I had it.

730
00:48:53,460 --> 00:48:55,560
I hate the king more than any of them.

731
00:48:56,220 --> 00:48:57,730
Don't say these things.

732
00:48:57,730 --> 00:48:59,000
If the wrong people hear you--

733
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:00,890
But you're not the wrong people.

734
00:49:06,930 --> 00:49:08,420
Don't trust anybody.

735
00:49:09,130 --> 00:49:10,720
Life is safer that way.

736
00:49:52,410 --> 00:49:54,280
And where are you going?

737
00:49:56,570 --> 00:49:59,010
I have something for you from Prince Theon.

738
00:49:59,010 --> 00:49:59,800
What?

739
00:50:00,330 --> 00:50:01,140
Me.

740
00:50:04,600 --> 00:50:06,630
He says I'm to make the rounds.

741
00:50:13,170 --> 00:50:15,070
And keep you warm.

742
00:50:42,780 --> 00:50:46,270
The Spice King refuses me because I'm a bad investment.

743
00:50:46,270 --> 00:50:47,770
The Silk King won't support me

744
00:50:47,770 --> 00:50:49,730
because of his business with the Lannisters.

745
00:50:49,730 --> 00:50:51,670
Why offend his best customer?

746
00:50:51,890 --> 00:50:55,430
And the Copper King offers me a single ship

747
00:50:55,430 --> 00:50:57,650
on the condition that I lie with him for a night.

748
00:50:58,200 --> 00:51:00,760
Does he think I will whore myself for a boat?

749
00:51:01,860 --> 00:51:04,820
When I came to this city, I had nothing.

750
00:51:05,380 --> 00:51:07,410
Truly nothing.

751
00:51:07,940 --> 00:51:09,580
I slept by the docks.

752
00:51:09,730 --> 00:51:12,430
And when I could find work loading the ships, I would eat.

753
00:51:12,790 --> 00:51:15,000
If not, I dreamed of food.

754
00:51:15,510 --> 00:51:18,180
Today I am the richest man in Qarth.

755
00:51:18,940 --> 00:51:21,040
Do you think the path from poverty to wealth

756
00:51:21,040 --> 00:51:23,770
is always pure and honorable?

757
00:51:24,600 --> 00:51:26,710
I have done many things, Khaleesi,

758
00:51:26,710 --> 00:51:28,570
that a righteous man would condemn.

759
00:51:29,930 --> 00:51:32,860
And here I am, with no regrets.

760
00:51:46,140 --> 00:51:49,160
Bar the gates. Ring the bells.

761
00:51:50,280 --> 00:51:51,640
Slowly, Khaleesi.

762
00:52:01,900 --> 00:52:03,100
Where are they?

763
00:52:10,590 --> 00:52:13,140
Where are my dragons?!

